    "explanation": "The disputed trip is TRP-02806, a METERED RYDE_X fare of SGD 21.10. The rider's case is that the route ran 14.84 km instead of the 14.0 km booked optimal, and both advocates agree on the governing figures: the trace distance is 14.84 km (EV-GPS-02806, weight 1.0), the booked optimal is 14.0 km (EV-TRIP-02806, weight 1.0), and the excess is 0.84 km, or 6.00% of optimal. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is BOTH greater than 20% of the optimal distance AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms. The absolute limb is cleared (0.84 > 0.8), but the percentage limb is not: 6.00% is far below the 20% the clause requires, and because the two limbs are conjunctive the threshold test fails. The clause then directs that no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The rider is right that the trace figure governs and not the rounded 14.8 km on the trip record — but the point does not help, because on the trace figure the percentage limb still fails, and on the rounded figure the absolute limb would fail as well (exactly 0.80 km, which must exceed 0.8). For the same reason the rider's conditional POL-RD-02 computation (charged_total 21.10, recomputed_fare 20.3920, refund 0.7080, i.e. SGD 0.75 payable) is never reached: POL-RD-02 runs only where a deviation is first established, and it is not. On the driver's side, the statement 'I followed the navigation' names no evidence ID and no traffic advisory covers this trip — EV-ADVIS-02806-01 is MISSING, carries weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — so under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13 it carries no weight; the rider's POL-RD-13 point is well taken, but it only removes an excuse the driver never needed, because the burden never shifted to him. Nothing separates the two sides' evidence on the threshold measurement. No billing-integrity defect exists to correct independently: the fare breakdown shows 0.00 ERP and tolls, an empty erp_gantries list, and a 0.00 airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, so POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to refund and produces no referral. The trace is clean for policy purposes — 117 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, maximum gap 0.0 s — so none of POL-RD-07's impairment limbs is met, POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged, and no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires; confidence is 0.95, comfortably above the 0.70 floor. The rider's profile check (deviation_claims_60d 0, deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0) confirms no heightened corroboration requirement attaches, and the profile was not used as a ground against either party. The outcome is NO_ACTION: the filing party's claim is not supported by the evidence, and the fare stands as charged (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0). No evidence was discarded and no claim was struck beyond the referee's own checks. The monetary effect is nil and therefore below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold; either party retains the appeal route under POL-GEN-04.",
