    "explanation": "To both parties: the fare of SGD 21.10 charged on trip TRP-02806 stands. No refund is due to the rider, no payment is due to the driver, and the payment state (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0) is left as it is.\n\nWhy there is no deviation. Under POL-RD-01 a route deviation is established only if the excess distance is BOTH more than 20% of the optimal distance AND more than 0.8 km in absolute terms. The governing measurement is the trace figure, gps_trace.trace_distance_km on EV-GPS-02806 = 14.84 km, not the rounded 14.8 km convenience copy on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02806), which POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test. Against the booked optimal of 14.0 km (EV-TRIP-02806) the excess is 0.84 km, i.e. 6.00% of optimal. It clears the 0.8 km limb by 0.04 km (the rounded 14.8 km would give exactly 0.80 km and would not clear it), but it falls far short of the 20% limb. Both limbs must pass, so no deviation is established and POL-RD-01 returns NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised.\n\nConsequently the rider's conditional request for a SGD 0.75 partial refund under POL-RD-02 is refused. The arithmetic is not in dispute — charged_total 21.10, recomputed_fare 20.3920, refund 0.7080 rounded up to 0.75, above the 0.50 de minimis — but POL-RD-02 only runs once a deviation is established under POL-RD-01, and the rider's own case properly concedes that the 20% limb is not met. The claim that the trace figure clears the absolute limb is correct and accepted, but on its own it does not establish a deviation.\n\nNo escalation is engaged. The trace is clean for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 117 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, an empty gaps array and a maximum consecutive-fix gap of 0.0 s, so none of limbs (a)–(c) fires and POL-RD-10(3) is not triggered; this is a case that can be ruled rather than deferred. No charge line is unmatched: ERP and tolls are 0.00, erp_gantries is empty, there is no airport surcharge, no surge uplift, no amended endpoint and no refund already issued, so POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to correct and POL-RD-10(8) has nothing to catch. POL-RD-10(5) is not triggered by the absent advisory either. The bundle holds EV-ADVIS-02806-01 as a MISSING traffic advisory at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and the driver's only account, 'I followed the navigation', names no evidence ID; under POL-RD-13 the driver's uncited traffic assertion is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else, and with that artifact absent the comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because the driver cites no artifact, the missing advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction in it, and no escalation follows from it. In any event the driver does not need the excuse: the rider never showed a threshold-meeting excess in the first place.\n\nOn the profiles: EV-RPROF-02806 records deviation_claims_60d 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0, so the heightened-corroboration condition in POL-RD-08 does not bite and no adverse inference is drawn. No profile field beyond those two citable counters affects this outcome, and POL-GEN-01 has been applied.\n\nFigures used: charged_total 21.10; optimal_distance_km 14.0; trace_distance_km 14.84; excess 0.84 km / 6.00%. The monetary effect is nil, which is below the execution threshold. The ruling is provisional and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
